  "novelty": "unknown",
  "construction": "Halving of the two-block code [[120,18,12]] (codes/120-18-12.json) along the fixed-point-free ZX-duality that exchanges (1,h) and (2,c-h) (symplectic halving: Lee, Okada, Maskara, Kasai, Zhou, arXiv:2609.30069, Def. 3; Burton, Durso-Sabina, Brown, arXiv:2406.09951); equivalently the mirror code of Khesin and Lu (arXiv:2603.05496) with A = c - F_B, B = F_A. Parent: G = Z/2 x Z/2 x Z/3 x Z/5, element (a,b,e,f) with index 30a+15b+5e+f; qubit (1,h) -> index of h, (2,h) -> 60 + index of h; X-check g on (1, g+F_A) and (2, g+F_B), Z-check g on (1, g-F_B) and (2, g-F_A), F_A = {(0,0,0,0),(0,0,1,1),(0,1,0,4),(1,0,2,4)}, F_B = {(0,0,0,0),(0,1,0,2),(0,1,2,4),(1,0,1,0)}; this is codes/120-18-12.json after renumbering G (the board file numbers G by GAP's Elements(SmallGroup(60,13))). Involution: Psi(1,h) = (2, c-h), Psi(2,h) = (1, c-h) with c = (1,0,0,0). Fold: fold qubit i is (1,h) with h of index i; the X-check g gives the generator with X on g+F_A and Z on c-g-F_B (Y where they meet), in the order of the X-checks. n = 60, rank 51, k = 9; 48 generators of weight 8 and 12 of weight 7; 12 Y factors, one in each of 12 generators; not locally Clifford equivalent to a CSS code.",
  "references": [
   "arXiv:2609.30069",
   "arXiv:2406.09951",
   "arXiv:2603.05496",
   "arXiv:2610.13880",
   "arXiv:2611.08247"
  ],
  "date": "2026-11-10",
  "model": "Claude Opus 5.5",
  "notes": "Distance 8 is exact: no nontrivial logical of Pauli weight <= 7 by three independent exhaustive computations (tropidist b03ec2d4077f in the board's Pauli encoding, certs/60-9-8.json in the same pull request; a meet-in-the-middle search of ours; Magma V2.30-1 MinimumDistance), and the witness has weight 8. Programs, data and logs: github.com/TimoKellerMath/quantum-error-correction @ 207d1130035a, folded-stabilizer-codes/. Not locally Clifford equivalent to a CSS code: the generator-level parity system for single-qubit Cliffords has no solution (qubit 3 carries X, Y and Z), and every generator is the only nontrivial stabilizer supported in its support, so no single-qubit Clifford makes the group CSS. At board commit 8042f9da no stabilizer entry dominates or equals it; it dominates the stabilizer entries 63-9-7 (on n and d) and 81-9-8 (on n). It is a mirror code of Khesin and Lu (arXiv:2603.05496) on Z/2 x Z/2 x Z/3 x Z/5 with |A| = |B| = 4; their code table has no codes of check weight 8, and in the sources of our literature check (the README of folded-stabilizer-codes/) we found no published code with the parameters [[60,9,8]] (codetables.de lists dense stabilizer codes with n = 60, k = 9 and d >= 12). Across code types the CSS entry 56-12-8 ([[56,12,8]], check weight 8) would dominate it; the board ranks the two types separately. Checked, not equivalent to an existing entry."
